{\b StreamMirror VR \emdash  unofficial community build}\par
\par
StreamMirror VR mirrors your VR view into OBS and window capture. It crops and steadies the picture, and can draw a ring where you look. Nothing it adds shows in the headset.\par
\par
{\b Updating from VR Gaze Mirror:} StreamMirror VR is its new name. Your settings come over, your OBS scenes keep their source, and Start with Windows stays on.\par
\par
Everything it installs is this project's own code (MIT licence):\par
\par
\bullet  {\b The OpenXR layers} \emdash  the mirror layer, which makes the picture in OpenXR games, and a small layer that tells the game's own panels from other tools'.\par
\bullet  {\b The quad views layer} \emdash  sharp where you look, cheaper elsewhere. It is installed switched off; the app's Quad Views page switches it on. It is built on Quad-Views-Foveated by Matthieu Bucchianeri (MIT licence). He did not build, test or endorse this package; please do not ask him for support with it.\par
\bullet  {\b The SteamVR helper} \emdash  makes the picture in games that use SteamVR directly. It uses Valve's OpenVR library (BSD licence).\par
\bullet  {\b The "StreamMirror VR" OBS plugin} \emdash  shows the picture in OBS (GPL-2, as OBS plugins are).\par
\bullet  {\b The mirror window and the settings app.}\par
\par
After installing, setup puts the OpenXR layer list in order, and saves the old order first.\par
\par
{\b Updating from 1.x:} setup removes the modified layers and the "OpenXR Mirror Capture" OBS plugin that 1.x installed. In your OBS scenes, replace that source with a "StreamMirror VR" source.\par
\par
Release builds are code-signed. Some games' anti-cheat software may still refuse OpenXR layers.\par
\par
The full licence texts are installed in the Licences folder next to the app.\par
